Z||000003||David Bartlett||09-29-2001||11:52 AM||||I would say its either the relay (very cheep to replace) or the large GEAR inside the motor casing.  If its the GEAR open the motor case, mark the gear and flip it around. The motor only uses half the teeth so you can get away with this.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||09-29-2001||02:02 PM||||When you turn the headlights on, do they headlights dance up and down but act like they don't have enough power to push the doors up on the hood or that a gear is stripped?<P>If so, replace the bushings. Rodney has them.<BR>$8<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||MontanaFiero||09-29-2001||06:20 PM||||Actually, they act like they don't even have power. I can effortlessly turn them up manually, but when the power is shut off, down they go.  <P>This is happening to BOTH of the lights, which is why I don't think it is the relay. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||09-29-2001||09:56 PM||||Replace the MAIN relay.||||reg||1
